<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  modules/renderer/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 2 module POM (Wave B)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/renderer -am package
  from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/renderer/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/renderer/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build;
  nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave B — renderer, javasci, graphic_export — the
  three modules whose only unmigrated-dependency risk (console, for
  renderer) was closed out by Wave A. The largest of Stage 2-f's remaining
  modules (67 source files) and the first to depend on scirenderer as a
  REACTOR SIBLING rather than a vendored jar (scirenderer migrated Stage
  2-d; every earlier module either predates it in the reactor or has no
  scirenderer dependency at all).

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh renderer, 67 files):
    [1] imports (excluding own packages):
      - com.jogamp.opengl.util — JoGLShapeDrawer usage; see the GLBuffers
        finding below.
      - org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath — real import, TeXConstants/TeXFormula/
        TeXIcon (grep-confirmed, JoGLView text-rendering code); NO jeuclid
        usage anywhere in this module (`grep -rn jeuclid modules/renderer/
        src/java` — zero hits), unlike modules/console/pom.xml which needs
        both. thirdparty/jlatexmath-1.0.7.jar, below.
      - org.scilab.forge.scirenderer{,.buffers,.clipping,.implementation.
        jogl,.lightning,.ruler{,.graduations},.shapes.{appearance,geometry},
        .texture,.tranformations,.utils.shapes.geometry} — scirenderer,
        below. THIS IS A REACTOR DEPENDENCY, not a vendored jar: scirenderer
        migrated to the Maven reactor in Stage 2-d
        (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2d-scirenderer.md) and has
        carried its own <finalName>scirenderer</finalName> POM ever since.
        Contrast modules/console/pom.xml and modules/helptools/pom.xml,
        both written before that migration existed for anything they used.
      - org.scilab.modules.commons{,.utils} — OS, utils.BlockingResult;
        org.scilab.modules.console.utils — ScilabSpecialTextUtilities
        (FormattedTextSpriteDrawer.java:23, TextObjectSpriteDrawer.java:33 —
        confirmed real imports, not comments); org.scilab.modules.
        graphic_objects{,.arc,.axes{,.Camera},.axis,.compound,
        .contouredObject,.datatip,.fec,.figure,.graphicController,
        .graphicObject{,.ClippableProperty},.graphicView,.imageplot,.label,
        .legend{,.Legend},.polyline,.rectangle,.surface,.textObject,
        .uicontrol.frame,.utils,.vectfield} plus two `import static`
        GraphicObjectProperties/Figure/Polyline members; org.scilab.modules.
        jvm — LoadClassPath (FormattedTextSpriteDrawer.java:27,
        TextObjectSpriteDrawer.java:37 — confirmed real imports);
        org.scilab.modules.localization — five reactor dependencies below,
        all already migrated (commons: Stage 2-b; console: Stage 2-f Task 1;
        graphic_objects: Stage 2-e; jvm: Stage 2-b; localization: Stage 2-a).
      - java.*, javax.swing{,.event,.tree} — JDK, not a dependency.
    [2] reflection targets: (none) — this module makes no Class.forName /
        loadClass call anywhere.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import: every name resolves to either
        the scirenderer packages above (org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.*, e.g.
        Canvas/Drawer/DrawingTools/SciRendererException/BuffersManager/...)
        or the graphic_objects packages above (e.g. MainDataLoader,
        ObjectRemovedException, PolylineData, ScilabNativeView, SurfaceData,
        Axes/AxesContainer/AxisProperty/Box, ColorMap/Figure, Grayplot/
        Matplot, Font/FormattedText/Text/TextObject, Arrow/Champ/Segs, ...),
        plus com.jogamp.opengl.util.GLBuffers (below) and one Messages
        (localization). Nothing new beyond [1]'s reactor set.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}" — same shape as modules/console/pom.xml
  and modules/helptools/pom.xml).

  THE GLBUFFERS FINDING — a second instance of the "inherited member" class
  helptools' xmlgraphics-commons finding documents, this time a superclass
  rather than a superinterface. renderer's own source has exactly one
  com.jogamp reference: `import com.jogamp.opengl.util` / GLBuffers.newDirect
  GLBuffer(...) (util/FormattedTextSpriteDrawer.java and others). `javap -p`
  on thirdparty/jogl-all-2.5.0.jar's own GLBuffers.class shows:
    public class com.jogamp.opengl.util.GLBuffers
        extends com.jogamp.common.nio.Buffers
  com.jogamp.common.* is GlueGen's namespace, not JOGL's — resolving
  GLBuffers' inherited members requires gluegen-rt's Buffers.class on the
  compile classpath even though renderer's source never spells
  com.jogamp.common.* out. build.incl.xml's compile.classpath puts both
  ${gluegen2.jar} (line 81) and ${jogl2.jar} (line 84) on every module's
  classpath unconditionally, consistent with this. Same two real Maven
  Central coordinates as modules/scirenderer/pom.xml's identical pair
  (cross-referenced, not restated — see that file's <dependencies> comment
  for the full systemPath-vs-alternatives rationale).
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>renderer</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:20 <property name="library.title" value="Plot management"/> -->
  <name>Plot management</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.OS, commons.utils.BlockingResult. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.console.utils.ScilabSpecialTextUtilities —
         FormattedTextSpriteDrawer.java, TextObjectSpriteDrawer.java. The
         wave's namesake edge (renderer<-console per the Stage 2-f plan);
         console migrated Stage 2-f Task 1 (Wave A). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>console</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.* — by far the widest single
         package family this module imports (arc, axes, axis, compound,
         contouredObject, datatip, fec, figure, graphicController,
         graphicObject, graphicView, imageplot, label, legend, polyline,
         rectangle, surface, textObject, uicontrol.frame, utils, vectfield).
         graphic_objects migrated Stage 2-e. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>graphic_objects</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.jvm.LoadClassPath — FormattedTextSpriteDrawer.
         java, TextObjectSpriteDrawer.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>jvm</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.* — this module's single widest
         dependency by import-line count (buffers, clipping, implementation.
         jogl, lightning, ruler(.graduations), shapes.(appearance,geometry),
         texture, tranformations, utils.shapes.geometry). A REACTOR SIBLING,
         not a vendored jar — see this file's header comment. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>scirenderer</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- THE JOGL / GLUEGEN PAIR — needed for com.jogamp.opengl.util.
         GLBuffers, whose OWN superclass (com.jogamp.common.nio.Buffers)
         lives in gluegen-rt, not jogl-all — see this file's header comment,
         "THE GLBUFFERS FINDING". SAME MECHANISM, SAME TWO REAL MAVEN
         CENTRAL COORDINATES AS modules/scirenderer/pom.xml (cross-
         referenced, not restated — see that file's <dependencies> comment
         for the full systemPath-vs-alternatives rationale, shared with
         modules/commons/pom.xml's flexdock comment). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.jogamp.jogl</groupId>
      <artifactId>jogl-all</artifactId>
      <version>2.5.0</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.jogamp.gluegen</groupId>
      <artifactId>gluegen-rt</artifactId>
      <version>2.5.0</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.{TeXConstants, TeXFormula, TeXIcon} —
         text-rendering code under JoGLView. Same jar, same coordinate as
         modules/console/pom.xml's identical dependency (cross-referenced,
         not restated). Only the plain jlatexmath jar is needed — renderer
         never touches org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.fop.* (the SEPARATE
         jlatexmath-fop.jar modules/helptools/pom.xml needs). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab.forge</groupId>
      <artifactId>jlatexmath</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.7</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/renderer/jar/org.scilab.modules.renderer.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carried (now un-mangled to "è" by register P1) the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
